---
source: crates/daemon/tests/integration/cli_help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Send a message, starting a conversation unless --conversation is given, and wait for the reply. Changes the assistant wants to make, and questions it asks, are printed with the command that answers them

Usage: mxr assistant send [OPTIONS] <MESSAGE>

Arguments:
  <MESSAGE>

Options:
      --conversation <CONVERSATION>  Continue this conversation
      --thread <THREAD>              The thread you mean by "this thread"
      --message <MESSAGES>           Messages you mean by "these" (repeatable)
      --no-wait                      Return as soon as the turn starts
      --format <FORMAT>              [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]
  -h, --help                         Print help
